# An error inside an `io.async` closure body (here a `String` passed to
# `exn.throw`, which takes `dyn(ToString + Error)`) is swallowed by the body's
# definition-time trial, and nothing evaluates that body again. Codegen then
# found it hollow and reported only the generic E0905, which never names the
# mistake
# (issues/fixed/an-ioasync-closure-calling-a-ctl-through-a-nested-bundle-field-ices-codegen.md).
# The trial now records what it swallowed, and codegen reports that error
# with its own code and span. A compiler with the bug scores a GOLDEN-DIFF
# (the E0905 line).
stdout_keep_match=(error\[E0601\]: Cannot unify incompatible types: "String" and "dyn\(ToString \+ Error\)"|error\[E0905\]|bad\.yo:[0-9]+:[0-9]+)
